<section class="da-section da-section--soft" aria-labelledby="deletion-details-title">
  <div class="da-shell">
    <header class="da-section__heading">
      <p class="da-overline">What deletion means</p>
      <h2 id="deletion-details-title">One sign-in can connect both Chakusa experiences</h2>
      <p>A Chakusa user may use the Customer experience, the Business experience, or both under the same authentication account. Deleting that user account affects every experience connected to it.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="da-detail-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Customer account</h3>
        <p>Your user profile and customer profile are deleted with their directly connected customer data, including customer preferences, saved activity, AI conversations, loyalty relationships, and other customer-profile records.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Business owner</h3>
        <p>If you still own a business, deleting your account deletes that business and its business-owned records. Deletion is blocked while other active team members remain. You can transfer ownership first and then delete only your own account, or remove the other members before deleting the business.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Business admin or staff</h3>
        <p>Deleting an admin or staff user removes that user's account and team membership. It does not delete the business tenant or the business owner's account.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Shared business records</h3>
        <p>Records controlled by a business, such as appointments, leads, messages, reviews, and payment activity, belong to that business. Some links to a deleted customer are removed while the business record remains.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="da-section" aria-labelledby="data-handling-title">
  <div class="da-shell da-data-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="da-overline">Data handling</p>
      <h2 id="data-handling-title">What is deleted and what may remain</h2>
      <p>Chakusa deletes the authenticated user record and data connected to it through the product's deletion rules. Business data is also deleted when the user is the remaining owner and the business is deleted.</p>
      <p>Minimal billing event records can remain without a link to the deleted business. These contain provider and transaction references used for billing reconciliation, not raw provider payloads or customer profiles.</p>
      <p>Some retention periods are not yet defined as fixed schedules. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for the current source of truth and contact the privacy team for a request about specific data.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="da-data-grid__aside">
      <h3>Subscriptions and billing</h3>
      <p>Deleting a Chakusa account does not automatically cancel an active subscription billed by Apple or Google.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Apple subscriptions must be managed in your Apple Account subscription settings.</li>
        <li>Google Play subscriptions must be managed in Google Play subscription settings.</li>
        <li>Cancel before renewal if you do not want the store subscription to continue.</li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
